  "question": {
    "text": "The maximum number of possible interference maxima for slit-separation equal to twice the wavelength in Young's double-slit experiment is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "OkIH6",
      "text": "\ninfinite\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "frMg8",
      "text": "\nfive\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "XuQhO",
      "text": "\nthree\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "aVeGH",
      "text": "\nzero",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "For interference maxima, $d \\sin \\theta=n \\lambda$\nHere $d=2 \\lambda$\n$\\therefore \\sin \\theta=\\mathrm{n} / 2$ and is satisfied by 5 integral values of $\\mathrm{n}(-2,-1,0,1,2)$, as the maximum value of $\\sin \\theta$ can only be 1 .",
    "image": null
  },
